  "voting_summary": "Maryland offers 8 days of early voting and no-excuse mail voting, with mail postmarked by election day accepted for 10 days. Polls close at 8 p.m. Eastern; early votes are released first, election day precincts report overnight, and the mail canvass then runs for more than a week, adding the most Democratic votes last: mail ran D+57 and late-counted mail D+66, against D+12 on election day. Maryland therefore shows one of the nation's strongest blue drifts after election night.",
